.TH FORGEKIT-INIT 1 "2026-08-25" "ForgeKit 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forgekit-init \- Initialize a new ForgeKit project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forgekit init
\fIproject-name\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize a new ForgeKit project with hexagonal architecture, PostgreSQL,
Docker Compose, database migrations, environment configuration, and tests.

The command interactively prompts for configuration unless
.B \-\-non-interactive
is specified.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-author \fIstring\fR
Project author name
.TP
.B \-\-db-name \fIstring\fR
PostgreSQL database name (default: project name with underscores)
.TP
.B \-\-dir \fIstring\fR
Target directory (default: project name)
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show the generation plan without writing to disk
.TP
.B \-\-module \fIstring\fR
Go module path (e.g., github.com/user/project)
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Run without interactive prompts (requires \fI\-\-module\fR)
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIint\fR
HTTP server port (default: 8080)
.TP
.B \-\-postgres-port \fIint\fR
PostgreSQL host port (default: 5432)
.TP
.B \-\-skip-postprocess
Skip gofmt and go test after generation
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce output (except errors and JSON)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive initialization:
.B forgekit init my-api
.TP
Non-interactive initialization:
.B forgekit init my-api --module github.com/example/my-api --port 8080 --non-interactive
.TP
Custom directory:
.B forgekit init my-api --dir /tmp/my-api
.TP
Preview without creating:
.B forgekit init my-api --dry-run
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error or invalid configuration
.TP
.B 2
Execution error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./forge.yaml
Project configuration (created)
.TP
.I ./.forge/features.yaml
Installed features tracking (created)
.TP
.I .env.example
Environment configuration template (created)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forgekit (1),
.BR forgekit-add (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ForgeKit Contributors <forgekit@demetrius-ch.github.io>